{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/949137-how-would-you-imagine-a-fight-between-two-powerful-splats-go","id":949137,"title":"How would you imagine a fight between two powerful splats go?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-11T22:44:00-07:00","id":949137,"title":"How would you imagine a fight between two powerful splats go?","content":"Say story wise- a Methuselah /Bodhisattva vampire encounters a Garou. The Garou recognize the vampire is tainted with wyrm and immediately attacks. Combat started. The two are indoors that has a lot of space. (Think a school auditorium).<br /> <br /> Would be a flashy Anime fight or different? I am trying to imagine how a fight of that caliber would play out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T23:44:55-07:00","id":949159,"title":"","content":"What rank is the Garou? What gifts does he have? What disciplines does the vampire have? <br /> <br /> If the Methuselah has 9 dots in Dominate and the Garou is only Rank 1, it's going to be a very short fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T01:43:41-07:00","id":949192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/949137-how-would-you-imagine-a-fight-between-two-powerful-splats-go?p=949159#post949159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What rank is the Garou? What gifts does he have? What disciplines does the vampire have?<br /> <br /> If the Methuselah has 9 dots in Dominate and the Garou is only Rank 1, it's going to be a very short fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>hmm I don't know much about the Garou. I assume it is just a standard Crinos Garou.<br /> <br /> For this match: Dominate can't be use. Only combat disciplines can be use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T02:09:41-07:00","id":949200,"title":"","content":"Its surprisingly unimpressive as whoever goes first kills the otherside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T02:14:02-07:00","id":949201,"title":"","content":"Yet another WhiteRoom splat-vs-splat Combat thread. These never end with a definitve answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> hmm I don't know much about the Garou. I assume it is just a standard Crinos Garou </div> </div> </div>There is no such thing. A Garou (and other Fera) have a Rank from 1 to 5, which allows them to use more powerful Gifts, not unlike Vampire Disciplines.<br /> <br /> If we are talking Methuselah, the opponent should be a Rank 5 Garou.<br /> At which point it depends on what Vampire Clan is facing which Werewolf Tribe, Auspice and Breed, and even on what merits/flaws they both have. And backgrounds.<br /> And the amount of Rage and Gnosis of the Garou. And if the Methuselah has Thaumaturgy/Necromancy/Koldunic paths or not.<br /> And once that all is established, it depends on how smart the players are, and if both sides had time to prepare or are suddenly tossed into the white room.<br /> <br /> White-Room combat is, most of the time, purely philosophical more so than practical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 08-12-2016, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T04:26:03-07:00","id":949230,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Go and test it by yourself: find a friend who knows well the Werewolf set up, create the character sheets for the methuselah and the Garou and play the same combat to the best of 3.<br /> <br /> Then change the Clan, the Tribe of the characters and the set up and test the combat again.<br /> <br /> It has to be fun to play.<br /> <br /> -I would say for the methuselah basic character sheet plus 700XP (Getting a clan discipline from 1 to 9 costs 180 XPs)<br /> -For the Rank 5 Garou basic character sheet plus 150 XP.<br /> -For the first set up I suggest both characters start face to face (no ambush) , in human form and all reserves (Blood, Rage, WP, Gnosis) are full.<br /> <br /> I guess the Vampire will win almost every time if she isn\u2019t ambushed.<br /> <br /> If you do share the results here.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T04:40:35-07:00","id":949237,"title":"","content":"I am not sure why people ride the 'Discipline level 9' idea here.<br /> 'Methuselah' is simply a Vampire that's older than about a millenium. Read: Embraced in 1015 AD would be enough.<br /> Lots of XP, probably Disciplines in the area of 6 to maaaaybe 7 dots, 7th or 6th Gen.<br /> <br /> Probably 7th Gen, if we are talking Player vs. Player Splat. So, Rank 6 disciplines max.<br /> <br /> 4th gen level 9 Discipline wielding monsters are a whole different category. Single Rank 5 Garou = dead. No contest. It's an ST-splat vs Player-Splat comparison. ST-Splat wins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 08-12-2016, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T05:53:20-07:00","id":949256,"title":"","content":"I can think of two reasons:<br /> <br /> 1) The first methuselah introduced in the world of darkens are Helena and Menele, so it\u2019s the age we usually give to methuselahs.<br /> 2) Because they\u2019re said to usually know the Antediluvians personally\u2026 and there were not Antediluvians walking around ot embracing people in the 1015 (Dark Ages). <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Methuselah\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Methuselah</a><br /> <br /> To be fair a methuselah has had to be embraced between the 1000 AD and Flood Myth (10.000 BC?). So we could say the average methuselah is 5500 years old.<br /> <br /> But, for the fight porpoises, test everything.<br /> The 700 XPs are for a vampire embraced around the year 0.<br /> If you want to run the test against a vampire embraced in the year 1000 AD, give him 350 or 400 XPs.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T06:28:01-07:00","id":949276,"title":"","content":"3 he slashed it with Bodhisattva which is always level 9 in a Dharma<br /> <br /> Really though as I said it will be profoundly unimpressive whoever goes first probably wins, unless the Vampire has a Nosell level of fortitude at which point Garou has blown his wad and is going to probably die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T06:54:42-07:00","id":949287,"title":"","content":"In the fluff, battles between extremely powerful opponents are often depicted as taking a long time. Like Ravnos and the elder Kuei-Jien going on for days or the fight between Mithras and the Garou pack taking all night. That sort of fight also appears in fiction, including fight that appear in ancient legends. Unfortunately, because of how WW combat rules work, things are weighted far more towards offense than defense. So the more powerful the opponents, the faster the fight will be over. So there is a good chance that a fight between a Methuselah and a Rank 5 Garou would take a single turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T07:06:13-07:00","id":949289,"title":"","content":"So, you are giving the vampire a 550 XP advantage? Unless they are designed by a moron, the vampire will always win just because of the XP advantage. A Methusalah would require a pack of Garou with 150 XP.<br /> <br /> A more fair comparison would be to compare beginning characters to beginning characters. In general, Werewolves are better than Vampires while Vampires are better than Changelings. Mages are supreme if they can prepare and die if they are caught by surprise. Wraiths generally are incapable of doing much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T07:30:45-07:00","id":949298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/949137-how-would-you-imagine-a-fight-between-two-powerful-splats-go?p=949287#post949287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the fluff, battles between extremely powerful opponents are often depicted as taking a long time. Like Ravnos and the elder Kuei-Jien going on for days or the fight between Mithras and the Garou pack taking all night. That sort of fight also appears in fiction, including fight that appear in ancient legends. Unfortunately, because of how WW combat rules work, things are weighted far more towards offense than defense. So the more powerful the opponents, the faster the fight will be over. So there is a good chance that a fight between a Methuselah and a Rank 5 Garou would take a single turn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ravana and Mithras have those crazy levels of fortitude that allow for serious No Selling. You might have to punch them all night for them to even notice..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T08:32:56-07:00","id":949329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/949137-how-would-you-imagine-a-fight-between-two-powerful-splats-go?p=949298#post949298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ravana and Mithras have those crazy levels of fortitude that allow for serious No Selling. You might have to punch them all night for them to even notice..</div> </div> </div> </div>Mithras only has 6 levels of Fortitude, so there are plenty of starting werewolves who can tank aggravated damage better than him. There is no way that Mithras could have stood up to a werewolf pack for more than a few turns without relying on his Presence or Dominate. As for Ravana, presumably his Fortitude does allow him to survive insane amounts of damage, but only because there are no rules for it. With all stated out characters offensive increases faster and more easily than defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 08-12-2016, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T08:34:52-07:00","id":949331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/949137-how-would-you-imagine-a-fight-between-two-powerful-splats-go?p=949329#post949329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mithras only has 6 levels of Fortitude, so there are plenty of starting werewolves who can tank aggravated damage better than him. There is no way that Mithras could have stood up to a werewolf pack for more than a few rounds without relying relying on his Presence or Dominate. As for Ravana, presumably his Fortitude does allow him to survive insane amounts of damage, but only because there are no rules for it. With all stated out characters offensive increases faster and more easily than defense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh I assumed Mithras had fortitude 9 and half a dozen out of clan disciplines probably including Assamite sorcery because.. what sort of god only has fortitude 6?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T08:43:49-07:00","id":949335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/949137-how-would-you-imagine-a-fight-between-two-powerful-splats-go?p=949331#post949331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh I assumed Mithras had fortitude 9 and half a dozen out of clan disciplines probably including Assamite sorcery because.. what sort of god only has fortitude 6?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is a link to Mithras, including his attributes.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Mithras\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Mithras</a><br /> <br /> he actually doesn't have many powerful Disciplines aside from Dominate 9 and Presence 8. Of course, those are enough to do really amazing things. If he saw a werewolf pack, he'd be like Cesar Millan. But if it came down to a purely physical fight, Mithras could be taken down by a single werewolf in a one on one fight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/949137-how-would-you-imagine-a-fight-between-two-powerful-splats-go?p=949289#post949289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you are giving the vampire a 550 XP advantage? Unless they are designed by a moron, the vampire will always win just because of the XP advantage. A Methusalah would require a pack of Garou with 150 XP.<br /> <br /> A more fair comparison would be to compare beginning characters to beginning characters. In general, Werewolves are better than Vampires while Vampires are better than Changelings. Mages are supreme if they can prepare and die if they are caught by surprise. Wraiths generally are incapable of doing much.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, this thread isn't about comparing who would win between a starting werewolf and vampire. That question has been addressed a million times before. This is a question about battles between epic characters like Methuselahs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T09:19:34-07:00","id":949350,"title":"","content":"There is nothing comparable to 4th Generation vampires except for, possibly, Archmages, so there is no comparison. How about you compare a 1000 years old 8th generation vampire to a fifth rank werewolf? That way, there is no 'Discipline versus Gift' shenanigans. Otherwise, a 7th generation vampire with Presence 6 just makes the Garou fall in love with her and turns him into her loyal guard dog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T10:26:37-07:00","id":949387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/949137-how-would-you-imagine-a-fight-between-two-powerful-splats-go?p=949350#post949350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is nothing comparable to 4th Generation vampires except for, possibly, Archmages, so there is no comparison. How about you compare a 1000 years old 8th generation vampire to a fifth rank werewolf? That way, there is no 'Discipline versus Gift' shenanigans. Otherwise, a 7th generation vampire with Presence 6 just makes the Garou fall in love with her and turns him into her loyal guard dog.</div> </div> </div> </div>Comparable to 4th Gen Vampires:<br /> Bodhisattvas<br /> The Silver Pack<br /> True Fae<br /> Silly statted out Fomori (or any Possessed)<br /> Bygones<br /> Archmages (who are generally better)<br /> Earthbound<br /> Powerful Jagglings<br /> <br /> I'm sure there are others, but those are off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> There are things comparable. They just generally get ignored by people who like to think of Methuselahs as unbeatable.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 08-12-2016, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T10:52:36-07:00","id":949409,"title":"","content":"No, I do not agree because they are not comparable. Even Bodhisattvas are not comparable because they simply do not have sufficient Chi storage to compete with Blood Pool storage of the 4th generation. Which Bygones and Jagglings are you talking about? Because I am pretty sure that any that made the mistake of materializing in front of a 4th generation would rapidly regret that mistake (a 4th generation vampire could potentially attack them ten times during the first turn, with 18 dice per attack, and deal 18 dice of aggravated damage per attack, plus successes). <br /> <br /> Let us take a look at what else 4th generation vampires are capable of. Create Name (Obfuscate 9) allows you to become someone completely different and, as long as you are not observe by someone with Auspex 9, your disguise is perfect. Psychic Assault (Auspex 8) allows you to instantly kill a target with five successes (not difficult for a 4th generation vampires since it is Manipulation plus Intimidation versus Willpower) and, even if the target resists, they lose half of their permanent Willpower, which would make the second use almost assured of instant death. Mythic Form (Protean 8) allows you to become a Dragon. And these are not the most broken or obscure powers that a 4th generation is capable of using.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T11:42:03-07:00","id":949444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/949137-how-would-you-imagine-a-fight-between-two-powerful-splats-go?p=949409#post949409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No, I do not agree because they are not comparable. Even Bodhisattvas are not comparable because they simply do not have sufficient Chi storage to compete with Blood Pool storage of the 4th generation. Which Bygones and Jagglings are you talking about? Because I am pretty sure that any that made the mistake of materializing in front of a 4th generation would rapidly regret that mistake (a 4th generation vampire could potentially attack them ten times during the first turn, with 18 dice per attack, and deal 18 dice of aggravated damage per attack, plus successes).</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, off the top of my head, Nexus Crawlers, Color Clouds and Strings, most Incarna Avatars. I'm not arguing who would win any given fight. just that they are comparable. And spitting out dice pools doesn't really matter since <i>most</i> Methuselahs can't actually do what you are attributing to any given Methuselah. <i>Some</i> can. Not all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/949137-how-would-you-imagine-a-fight-between-two-powerful-splats-go?p=949409#post949409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Let us take a look at what else 4th generation vampires are capable of. Create Name (Obfuscate 9) allows you to become someone completely different and, as long as you are not observe by someone with Auspex 9, your disguise is perfect. Psychic Assault (Auspex 8) allows you to instantly kill a target with five successes (not difficult for a 4th generation vampires since it is Manipulation plus Intimidation versus Willpower) and, even if the target resists, they lose half of their permanent Willpower, which would make the second use almost assured of instant death. Mythic Form (Protean 8) allows you to become a Dragon. And these are not the most broken or obscure powers that a 4th generation is capable of using.</div> </div> </div> </div>Create Name doesn't matter for a fight. Psychic Assault isn't going to get 5 successes against a comparable foe. Mythic Form adds 9 to attributes and some stuff here and there and so is (maybe) slightly better than some Mokole's archid and really isn't all that impressive (plus it takes at least a full turn to change into).<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Sample Mythic Form: Dragon</b><br /> +3 Strength, +2 Dexterity, +4 Stamina. Flight at normal running movement rate. Three dice of armor usable against aggravated damage. Bite and claw attacks at Strength +2 aggravated damage. Fiery breath as per standard ranged attack above.&quot;<br /> <br /> Again, I'm not saying Methuselahs are weak by any means. But there are certainly comparable power levels running around the WoD.<br /> <br /> oh...adding to my list above:<br /> Thunderwyrms and Zmei.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T13:13:46-07:00","id":949484,"title":"","content":"I do not know, the Great Zmei tend to be relatively weak in comparison to 4th generation vampires. Considering that a 4th generation vampire should have 16-18 dice in their primary die pools (look at Baba Yoga) but the Great Zmei tend to average 10 dice on their primary die pools (see Rage Across Russia). Of course, if one of the Great Zmei hits it, even a 4th generation vampire may regret its existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T13:34:26-07:00","id":949502,"title":"","content":"One of the problems in this sort of discussion is that everyone is inevitably discussing a sort of &quot;Schrodinger Methuselah&quot; - a Methuselah who has a theoretical 9 dots in every Attribute and every Ability and every Discipline. Such a Methuselah could demolish just about anything but at the same time such a Methuselah doesn't actually exist. Still, as long as everyone has their own internal idea for what stats a &quot;Methuselah&quot; has, I doubt you'll see any kind of agreement on their capabilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T13:34:36-07:00","id":949503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/949137-how-would-you-imagine-a-fight-between-two-powerful-splats-go?p=949484#post949484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not know, the Great Zmei tend to be relatively weak in comparison to 4th generation vampires. Considering that a 4th generation vampire should have 16-18 dice in their primary die pools (look at Baba Yoga) but the Great Zmei tend to average 10 dice on their primary die pools (see Rage Across Russia). Of course, if one of the Great Zmei hits it, even a 4th generation vampire may regret its existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>3 Gnosis rips a hole to Malfeas. Dice pools really aren't everything. Baba Yaga is on the higher end of power levels for Methuselahs. I wouldn't assume every Methuselah has a 16-18 dice pool either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/949137-how-would-you-imagine-a-fight-between-two-powerful-splats-go?p=949502#post949502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the problems in this sort of discussion is that everyone is inevitably discussing a sort of &quot;Schrodinger Methuselah&quot; - a Methuselah who has a theoretical 9 dots in every Attribute and every Ability and every Discipline. Such a Methuselah could demolish just about anything but at the same time such a Methuselah doesn't actually exist. Still, as long as everyone has their own internal idea for what stats a &quot;Methuselah&quot; has, I doubt you'll see any kind of agreement on their capabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this 100%. &quot;Comparable power levels&quot; to me is a very broad range. These are after all damn near (and sometimes really are) plot device power levels being discussed.<br /> Even when these types of beings do have stats, the stats don't usually account for all of the feats attributed to said creature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 08-12-2016, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T13:54:17-07:00","id":949510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/949137-how-would-you-imagine-a-fight-between-two-powerful-splats-go?p=949484#post949484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not know, the Great Zmei tend to be relatively weak in comparison to 4th generation vampires. Considering that a 4th generation vampire should have 16-18 dice in their primary die pools (look at Baba Yoga) but the Great Zmei tend to average 10 dice on their primary die pools (see Rage Across Russia). Of course, if one of the Great Zmei hits it, even a 4th generation vampire may regret its existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Revised, the Zmei were not given a stat reprint, and it was sort of assumed from the tone of the writing that they were far, far more powerful than what was detailed in RAR. Baba Yaga basically accessed a plot device before the Embrace took hold and used it to get a few things on her side that hit above her new, now-vampiric weight class; Absimilard only managed to avoid destruction through misdirection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T17:14:54-07:00","id":949646,"title":"","content":"When people say Methuselah i tend to think Baba Yaga, Ur Shulgi, Shaitan etc rather than Vykos, Lucita (those guys may be 1000 years old, but they are not Methuselahs).<br /> <br /> If we look at Shaitans <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Huitzilopochtli_(VTM)#Character_Sheet\" target=\"_blank\">stats</a>, Baba Yagas <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Baba_Yaga#Character_Sheet\" target=\"_blank\">stats</a> and Ur Shulgis <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Ur-Shulgi#Character_Sheet\" target=\"_blank\">stats</a>, we can see that even a Rank 6 Garou would have problem taking them down. Even with younger Methuselahs like <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Karsh#Character_Sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Karsh</a> would probably give a Garou Elder a run for his money.<br /> <br /> Edit: I know that i just contradicted myself by naming Karsh (embraced 12th Century AD) as a Methuselah while saying that Vykos and Lucita aren't. Maybe it's the fact that Karsh is 5th gen...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T17:51:18-07:00","id":949662,"title":"","content":"This question is like asking who would win in a money throwing fight - Scrooge McDuck or three regular ducks in a trenchcoat. One has a few HUGE advantages over the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T18:32:03-07:00","id":949684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/949137-how-would-you-imagine-a-fight-between-two-powerful-splats-go?p=949646#post949646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we look at Shaitans <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Huitzilopochtli_(VTM)#Character_Sheet\" target=\"_blank\">stats</a>, Baba Yagas <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Baba_Yaga#Character_Sheet\" target=\"_blank\">stats</a> and Ur Shulgis <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Ur-Shulgi#Character_Sheet\" target=\"_blank\">stats</a>, we can see that even a Rank 6 Garou would have problem taking them down. Even with younger Methuselahs like <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Karsh#Character_Sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Karsh</a> would probably give a Garou Elder a run for his money.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's at least why I put the Silver Pack as comparable. 5+ Garou of Rank 5+ would compare a bit better. Certainly not an ensured victory (quite possibly not even possible, depending on conditions). But a lot better than comparing a random Garou (even a Legend) to a several thousand year old 4th-5th gen Vampire.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T18:58:23-07:00","id":949693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/949137-how-would-you-imagine-a-fight-between-two-powerful-splats-go?p=949646#post949646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When people say Methuselah i tend to think Baba Yaga, Ur Shulgi, Shaitan etc rather than Vykos, Lucita (those guys may be 1000 years old, but they are not Methuselahs).<br /> <br /> If we look at Shaitans <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Huitzilopochtli_(VTM)#Character_Sheet\" target=\"_blank\">stats</a>, Baba Yagas <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Baba_Yaga#Character_Sheet\" target=\"_blank\">stats</a> and Ur Shulgis <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Ur-Shulgi#Character_Sheet\" target=\"_blank\">stats</a>, we can see that even a Rank 6 Garou would have problem taking them down. Even with younger Methuselahs like <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Karsh#Character_Sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Karsh</a> would probably give a Garou Elder a run for his money.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really? Just having high Honor or Virtue Renown at Rank 2 can allow you to boost your physical Attributes to ridiculous heights with Fu Xi's Honor/Rage of the Nest Mother. Fire can be seriously downgraded by starting characters, the the lower-ranked Garou might turn the battlefield into a sea of flames accordingly and just deal with the bashing damage that they take.<br /> <br /> Actual high-Rank Gifts? That'd be a much tougher nut to crack. Legendary characters can be arbitrarily immune to mind control and able to free others, in addition to lower-ranked effects that are still actually quite impressive, like being able to make the enemy whiff as long as they don't attack, or making an imaginary monster that can hit harder than any vampire with stats can withstand. There is no limit on the number of successes that you can pump into Fabric of the Mind, or how high the dream-being's stats can be; If you're just sitting around, you can keep rolling for it every turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T19:51:34-07:00","id":949733,"title":"","content":"Intelligence plus Performance (difficulty 8) means that, on ten dice, you will average 3 successes per roll (assuming two successes on a 10 in your specialty). You will botch within 20 rolls or so, in which the creature is out of your control, and will stick around as long as it wants. You can give it 60 dots in traits, which makes it equal to a werewolf, but it costs one Gnosis per turn of combat. It is hardly a superstar ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T14:40:32-07:00","id":950228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/949137-how-would-you-imagine-a-fight-between-two-powerful-splats-go?p=949733#post949733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Intelligence plus Performance (difficulty 8) means that, on ten dice, you will average 3 successes per roll (assuming two successes on a 10 in your specialty). You will botch within 20 rolls or so</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how probability works. There's a noticeably increased chance of botching, not an absolute certainty of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> in which the creature is out of your control, and will stick around as long as it wants. You can give it 60 dots in traits, which makes it equal to a werewolf, but it costs one Gnosis per turn of combat. It is hardly a superstar ability. </div> </div> </div>No, one dot per scene no matter what; so says W20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T15:33:48-07:00","id":950262,"title":"","content":"I understand statistics, I am a professional analyst and researcher, the likelihood of a cumulative probability of a botch exceeds 90% after 20 rolls or so. At that point, you have a really powerful creature not under your control, which may be a problem. If you are lucky, it is peaceful and curious. If you designed a monster, you may have issues, especially if it's combat traits exceed your combat traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T18:22:33-07:00","id":951417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/949137-how-would-you-imagine-a-fight-between-two-powerful-splats-go?p=950262#post950262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand statistics, I am a professional analyst and researcher, the likelihood of a cumulative probability of a botch exceeds 90% after 20 rolls or so. At that point, you have a really powerful creature not under your control, which may be a problem. If you are lucky, it is peaceful and curious. If you designed a monster, you may have issues, especially if it's combat traits exceed your combat traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not everything can be Dance of Shiva, apparently.<br /> <br /> (Rank 6 Nagah gets 22 success, Rank 6 Nagah literally sets the entire surface of the planet Earth aflame for up to 25 dice of aggravated damage).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T18:36:06-07:00","id":951423,"title":"","content":"Well, that would actually be resisted by every sorcerer with Spirit Counterspell, so it would probably only torch a few square miles before there are sufficient counterspell successes to cancel it. I do not think that you could get 22 successes off of a maximum die pool of 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 08-15-2016, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T18:44:35-07:00","id":951426,"title":"","content":"An arguably more effective, and slightly more likely to encounter Gift, would be the level five Breath of the Dragon. The Nagah could potentially do 12 dice of aggravated damage with each attack, with no restrictions, at a range of 20 yards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T21:47:28-07:00","id":951493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/949137-how-would-you-imagine-a-fight-between-two-powerful-splats-go?p=949662#post949662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This question is like asking who would win in a money throwing fight - Scrooge McDuck or three regular ducks in a trenchcoat. One has a few HUGE advantages over the other.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Scrooge is less likely to carry large sums of money on him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T22:09:40-07:00","id":951503,"title":"","content":"Less likely than three regular ducks in a trenchcoat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T02:32:18-07:00","id":951568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/949137-how-would-you-imagine-a-fight-between-two-powerful-splats-go?p=951503#post951503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Less likely than three regular ducks in a trenchcoat?</div> </div> </div> </div>where'd the trenchcoat come from? Hell they may have a Katana older than Katanas with the right coat!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T19:12:29-07:00","id":952208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/949137-how-would-you-imagine-a-fight-between-two-powerful-splats-go?p=951423#post951423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that would actually be resisted by every sorcerer with Spirit Counterspell, so it would probably only torch a few square miles before there are sufficient counterspell successes to cancel it. I do not think that you could get 22 successes off of a maximum die pool of 10.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they wouldn't, because they would have to make an elaborate ritual to target said level six Gift, whereas all the Nagah needs is to keep dancing for about a minute; by the time they realize what's up, they're already dead (each turn, the circle of flames doubles its radius and adds one to damage, from a start at ten years and three dice; you can only dance for a number of turns equal to the successes rolled). And 22 successes is possible with a specialty and the Gift that makes Willpower spent count as two successes rather than one (Stargazer Rank 1). The probability is exactly 1/10^10, which is a very long shot, of course, but technically possible, and even &quot;near misses&quot; about that sum can still wreck a very large area.<br /> <br /> Bonus? It costs nothing. No Gnosis, no Rage, no Willpower, though obviously the Wani would likely frown on one of Gaia's judges causing widespread devastation. The only ones getting out of that inferno are the truly virtuous or innocent, which the Gift lays out as really fucking rare in the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T19:26:31-07:00","id":952212,"title":"","content":"No, a normal counterspell may be cast instantly (Sorcerer: The Hedge Wizard's Handbook, p. 87), so a sorcerer would abort to one as soon as they sensed it through Awareness. And there is no way that much magic would not be sensed across the Earth, meaning that every magic user on Earth (mage, sorcerer, etc) would attempt to counterspell it and would likely move Heaven and Earth to destroy anything that powerful. There are checks and balances, even in the World of Darkness, if you know where to look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T05:14:01-07:00","id":952438,"title":"","content":"Yeah, due to the fact that counterspelling cuts successes even if it can't counter the power entirely. It's worth to note, however, that the countering mages will have to know how to counter Gifts. This isn't automatic, Sorcerer's need a special countermagic for each different kind of magick, and mages need specific Spheres and, maybe, Spirit 4.<br /> <br /> It's also a Storyteller fiat more than a rule to say that &quot;Awareness will be applied automatically with such a potent magick&quot;. The Storyteller has to decide if an automatic Awareness check it's appropiate with such a potent magic, and if it can discern the nature of the danger with enough pressicion (knowing that &quot;powerful magick it's coming&quot; it's not enough to prepare a counterspell, if you don't know the kind).<br /> It's like arguing that Time 2 mages are going to investigate such an event and stop it before it happens. Or self-conscious Incarna that have ties with humanity. Or Antediluvians who may not want to have humans (the best source of vampires) anihilated. Or Garou that can predict disasters. Or Demons. Yeah, someone it's going to stop you, but that's a storyteller fiat at the end of the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T19:00:12-07:00","id":952918,"title":"","content":"Sometimes, ST fiat is the only way to produce plausible results when players wants to do stupid things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T22:58:01-07:00","id":953001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/949137-how-would-you-imagine-a-fight-between-two-powerful-splats-go?p=952918#post952918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes, ST fiat is the only way to produce plausible results when players wants to do stupid things.</div> </div> </div> </div>ST fiat in this case would probably channel the destruction into a more local area and up the damage rather than expanding its range. Because, again, while the powers of the Wani do invoke some pretty heinous feats of destruction akin to volcanoes and storms, the Nagah should have more measured attacks. It was just written carelessly (and when it was written, it was technically possible to increase the range even further, albeit much less likely, since it would rely on exploding 10s).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T05:00:44-07:00","id":953101,"title":"","content":"Yes, the probability of 22 successes would have been much lower, around 1 in 10,000,000,000,000 rather than 1 in 10,000,000,000.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}